### Title
OOB

### Severity
High

### Difficulty
Low

### Type
Data Exposure

### Target
Pwnable Source/ShellCode_Required/socket_bof.c

## Description
the str not only can overwrite the stack data, but also doesn't have to end with 0. If it doesn't and attacker has access to standard output, he could read data from stack.

## Exploit Scenario
Attacker sends a meesage not terminated with 0, sprintf does it's job and now we print out "Sent back -  {data}" directly to standard output.

## Recommendations
when receiving str from socket, terminate it with 0 by resading only 499 bytes and adding 0 to end or print out 500 bytes at max using printf("Sent back - %.500s", str). The best way is to use both.


